<h2>Cancelling and refunds</h2>
<p>These terms apply to everything bought from {{ business }}. They set out
when you can change your mind, and what happens when you do.</p>

{% if sells_physical %}
<h3>Things we post to you</h3>
<p>You can cancel for any reason within {{ withdrawal_days }} days of receiving
your order, without giving a reason. Tell us at <a href="mailto:{{ email }}">{{ email }}</a>
and send the item back within {{ withdrawal_days }} days of telling us. We refund
what you paid, including standard delivery, within 14 days of getting the item
back. Return postage is yours to pay unless the item was faulty or not what you
ordered.</p>
<p>Items must come back in a condition where we could reasonably sell them
again. Handling them as you would in a shop is fine; using them is not.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if sells_digital %}
<h3>Downloads</h3>
<p>A download normally carries the same {{ withdrawal_days }}-day right to change
your mind. Because a file cannot be given back once it has been sent, that right
ends the moment your download starts &mdash; and by starting it you agree to
that, and accept that you are giving up the right to cancel.</p>
<p>If a file is faulty, will not open, or is not what was described, tell us at
<a href="mailto:{{ email }}">{{ email }}</a> and we will fix it or refund you.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if sells_services %}
<h3>Sessions and appointments</h3>
<p>You can cancel a booking up to {{ booking_notice_hours }} hours before it
starts, and the session goes back to your account for you to rebook whenever
suits. Cancel later than that, or miss the appointment, and the session is
used.</p>
<p>Unused sessions can be refunded within {{ withdrawal_days }} days of purchase,
less the value of any session already taken. If you asked us to start sooner
than that and the work is finished, the right to cancel no longer applies.</p>
{% endif %}

<h3>If something goes wrong</h3>
<p>Nothing here affects your legal rights when something is faulty, misdescribed,
or not delivered. Email <a href="mailto:{{ email }}">{{ email }}</a> and we will
sort it out.</p>
{% if in_eu %}
<p>If we cannot agree, you can use the European Commission's online dispute
resolution platform at
<a href="https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr" rel="noopener">ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr</a>.</p>
{% endif %}
